  "$comment_check_strategy": "check_strategy selects how a scope is verified: exact (one predictor, exact comparison), composed (chained predictors down a feed-forward path), invariant (legality rules — used where many orderings are legal, so prediction would fail against correct RTL), observe (autonomous DUT; monitors and SVA carry the check). Read as data by the orchestrator; never inferred from a scope name.",
  "$comment_stimulus": "stimulus_generator names the directed generator for the path (register_walk, status_poll, refresh_stress); absent means constrained-random on the entry stream (register_walk for a CSR entry at seed 1). window_cycles is the observation window for a path with no driver; settle_cycles the drain after the driver finishes.",
  "$comment_judged_in": "judged_in: a single-hop path whose check is exactly one stage of a longer path's run. run_path.py writes a derived report for it whenever the host path is judged, so every path has a report and every downstream tool (compare_drops, the fault matrix, the cockpit) sees all of them as first-class."
